      choices: ["Yes, always", String.raw`No: $D$ is the center of the circle through $A$, $B$, $C$, so it is not on that circle`, String.raw`Only if triangle $ABC$ is equilateral`, "Only if the quadrilateral is convex"],
      answer: "B",
      solution: String.raw`$D$ is equidistant from $A$, $B$, $C$, so it is the circumcenter of triangle $ABC$: the center of the only circle through the three points, at distance $5$ from each, and at distance $0$ from itself. The center of a circle is not on it, so the four points are not concyclic. Equal distances from $D$ make $A$, $B$, $C$ concyclic with center $D$; they say nothing about $D$ being on the circle.`
