      answer: "D", prompt: "Enter the letter of your choice.",
      solution: String.raw`Equal arcs have equal chords, so exactly one pair of opposite sides is equal, say $AD=BC$ with $AB\ne CD$. Equal arcs $AD$ and $BC$ give equal inscribed angles $\angle ABD=\angle BDC$, which are alternate angles for the lines $AB$ and $CD$ cut by $BD$, so $AB\parallel CD$. If $AD\parallel BC$ too, $ABCD$ would be a cyclic parallelogram, hence a rectangle ({{ref:cor-shapes}}), with both pairs of opposite sides equal. So exactly one pair of sides is parallel: an isosceles trapezoid. The most specific choice offered is (D), trapezoid.`
