      solution: String.raw`$B$ and $C$ see segment $AD$ under equal angles from the same side, so $ABCD$ is cyclic by the {{ref:thm-equal}}. Inside the circle, $\angle BAC$ and $\angle BDC$ stand on the same arc $BC$, so they are equal. Opposite angles add to $180^\circ$; they are not equal in general, and no side lengths follow.`
